        "title": "Plastic Deformation and Work Hardening",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Plastic deformation changes the shape of a metal permanently by moving dislocations through the crystal lattice. The interaction between dislocations — and between dislocations and other microstructural features — determines why metals get harder when deformed (work hardening) and how to undo that hardening (annealing)."
